 "intro": {
  "text": "In the Italian Game White puts the bishop on c4, where it controls d5 and eyes f7, the weakest pawn in Black's camp, and gets ready to castle early. After 3...Bc5, the Giuoco Piano or \"quiet game\", White's classical plan is to build a big pawn centre with c3 and d4.",
