     "notes": {
      "text": "2...Nc6 defends e5. White usually develops the bishop next, keeping c3 and d4 in reserve. 3.Bc4, the Italian Game, aims it at Black's weak f7 pawn. 3.Bb5 (Spanish) pressures the knight that guards e5, and 3.d4 (Scotch) opens the centre at once. 3.Nxe5?? simply gives away a knight.",
