     "notes": {
      "text": "Black controls d4 three times to your two, so 4.c3 adds a defender and prepares d4. 4.d3 is the quieter Giuoco Pianissimo, 4.d4 at once is a gambit that is not quite sound, and 4.b4 is the Evans Gambit. Avoid 4.Bxf7+?: the Jerome Gambit comes far too early and is objectively bad for White.",
